From: hhm123 <hhm123@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 10:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hailo15-isp: ratelimit the AFM overflow message

The AFM overflow warning in hailo15_isp_handle_int() is printed
unconditionally for every frame whose ISP_MIS raises
ISP_MIS_AFM_SUM_OF / ISP_MIS_AFM_LUM_OF. On scenes with strong
illumination (direct sun at noon, IR-LED reflection at night) the
overflow bit stays asserted on ~83% of frames, which floods the
journal at ~25 lines/s (measured 343k lines overnight, rotating
away boot logs at a 204 MB journal cap). The overflow itself is
benign for the AF algorithm: the AFM sum statistics remain valid
and autofocus confidence is unaffected.

Guard the print with a private ratelimit state of one message per
minute (not the shared printk_ratelimit() state, so an AFM flood
cannot starve other drivers' ratelimited diagnostics).

Measured on hailo15-ne503: 25 msg/s before, 1 msg/min after; AF
windows/stats and autofocus (confidence 0.999) unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: hhm123 <hhm123@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/hailo15-isp-hw.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/hailo15-isp-hw.c b/drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/hailo15-isp-hw.c
index 2cd66e1..d398b58 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/hailo15-isp-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/hailo/hailo15/hailo15-isp-hw.c
@@ -1533,6 +1533,13 @@ static void hailo15_isp_handle_mcm_raw_write_irq(struct hailo15_isp_device *isp_
 	}
 }

+/* AFM statistics overflow is expected under strong illumination (direct
+ * sun, night IR reflection) and is benign for the AF algorithm; the raw
+ * per-frame print floods the log at frame rate, so report at most once
+ * a minute via a private state (not the shared printk_ratelimit one).
+ */
+static DEFINE_RATELIMIT_STATE(afm_overflow_rs, 60 * HZ, 1);
+
 static void hailo15_isp_handle_int(struct hailo15_isp_device *isp_dev)
 {
 	int event_size = 0;
@@ -1597,8 +1604,9 @@ static void hailo15_isp_handle_int(struct hailo15_isp_device *isp_dev)

 	if (isp_dev->irq_status.isp_mis &
 	    (ISP_MIS_AFM_SUM_OF | ISP_MIS_AFM_LUM_OF)) {
-		pr_warn("%s - AFM overflow - mis = 0x%x\n", __func__,
-			isp_dev->irq_status.isp_mis);
+		if (__ratelimit(&afm_overflow_rs))
+			pr_warn("%s - AFM overflow - mis = 0x%x\n", __func__,
+				isp_dev->irq_status.isp_mis);
 	} else if (isp_dev->irq_status.isp_mis & (ISP_MIS_AFM_FIN)) {
 		if (stream_exists) {
 			irq_deffered_work = kzalloc(sizeof(struct hailo15_irq_deffered_work), GFP_ATOMIC);
--
2.34.1
